{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_context_dictionary", "label": "Dictionary capability context", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/context/dictionary.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dictionary workflows parse Bosworth-Toller into bt_* lookup tables, relink morphology forms.entry_id after each rebuild, and expose query and browse. Startup readiness only guarantees schema, so empty bt_* tables after migrate are expected until build runs, while dictionary query requires populated bt_entries, bt_senses, and bt_variants. Homographs that share a normalized key and part of speech stay separate blocks. Wright prose is not ingested by dictionary build."}, {"id": "bundled_oe_bt_txt", "label": "Bundled Bosworth-Toller source oe_bt.txt", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/context/dictionary.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dictionary build reads wyrdcraeft/etc/dictionary/oe_bt.txt by default into bt_* tables. The diacritic ADRs also call the bundled oe_bt.txt the variant source for the macron index, which is repaired from it and not regenerated, because the index holds curation the plain text does not."}, {"id": "forms_entry_relinker", "label": "FormsEntryRelinker", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/context/dictionary.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After each dictionary rebuild every forms.entry_id is cleared and recomputed. Ambiguous or missing joins leave entry_id NULL so morphology forms are not attached to the wrong dictionary entry."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_context_dictionary", "target": "docs_context_morphology", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/context/dictionary.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source":